\ File-output report checks do not invoke expensive date calculations.
\ They exercise the same formatter the explicit output entrypoint
\ uses after either success or failure.

To check the public date report:
  Put 1 into the complete date status.
  Put 5000 into the complete date answer's year number.
  Put 10 into the complete date answer's cutlet name index.
  Put 503 into the complete date answer's day within cutlet.
  Put 20 into the complete date answer's month name index.
  Put 56 into the complete date answer's day within month.
  Prepare the calendar date report.
  If the calendar date report is not "5000, Scorpion, 503, Well, 56",
    put "A successful date did not yield readable output." into the check report; exit.
  Put 0 into the complete date status.
  Put "Sample failure reason." into the complete date error.
  Prepare the calendar date report.
  If the calendar date report is not "Sample failure reason.",
    put "A failed date report did not explain the failure." into the check report; exit.
  Put 1 into the complete date status.
  Put 48 into the complete date answer's month name index.
  Prepare the calendar date report.
  If the calendar date report is not "The calculated date could not be given its English names.",
    put "An unknown calendar name did not cause a safe error." into the check report; exit.
  Reset the complete date answer.
